Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Model 1: Plotting", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9175337932598257`*^9, 3.917533797250618*^9}, {
  3.9616150156067543`*^9, 
  3.961615015745549*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"18470d13-502e-4393-bbc6-\
041671e0a9ad"],

Cell["\<\
This file contains the processing code for Model 1: Effects of \
Autocorrelation Across the Thermal Landscape. Before running this file, you \
must have extinction time outputs from running Model 1 on a TPC using \
Model1.nb; edit import and export locations (via \[OpenCurlyQuote]saveto\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]) for your own device.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9175338428119698`*^9, 3.9175339656794977`*^9}, {
  3.917608589465108*^9, 3.9176086415654793`*^9}, {3.961614986430071*^9, 
  3.961615013537793*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"73a9ddb7-f46e-4be2-b733-\
504598acc234"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Load Data", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.917534034690617*^9, 
  3.9175340372370453`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"deab0e70-73c9-49f6-a4ea-\
8375620460f1"],

Cell["\<\
Run import code before creating any figures. Edit the import/export file \
names/locations for your local system and, if necessary, edit loaded \
parameter space to match your imported run. Default size is \
tmax2000_dims21,7,7,1000, corresponding with 1000 runs of 2000 time steps at \
each of 21 autocorrelation levels, 7 mean temperatures, and 7 standard \
deviations of temperature. Choose outputs for either the temperate or the \
tropical TPC. Subfigures from this file were combined using Adobe Illustrator \
2024.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9175340603643427`*^9, 3.917534170031529*^9}, {
  3.917534371989325*^9, 3.917534382734783*^9}, {3.91753518488971*^9, 
  3.91753525860928*^9}, {3.958056379946052*^9, 3.9580564294673147`*^9}, {
  3.961615037293071*^9, 
  3.961615038347735*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6c15f114-b061-4f48-b0a9-\
2542a346eb02"],

